course: dictionary
lesson: 10871
title: One word, many views
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word view has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one is meant. «The hotel room had a view of the sea.» Here a view is the scene you can see from a place, so it is a noun.
explain: «Move, you're blocking my view!» Here view means the ability to see something from where you are. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a scene, or about being unable to see?
explain: View can also be a verb, meaning to look at something or to think about it in a certain way. «She views it as a challenge» means she thinks of it as a challenge. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: «In my view, the plan will work» uses view to mean an opinion. Try swapping in opinion: «In my opinion, the plan will work» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: View can be a noun (a view, views) or a verb (view, viewed, viewing).
fact: «View» can mean what you can see from a place, especially a lovely scene.
fact: «In my view» means «I think», so view can mean an opinion.
fact: «To view» means to look at something, or to think about it in a certain way.
fact: In maths, a front view, side view or plan view shows how a 3-D shape looks from one side or from above.
exercise: «The hotel room had a view of the sea.» In this sentence, what does view mean? | A way of cooking fish | To think about something | A small boat | *What you can see from a place
exercise: «In my view, the plan will work.» What does view mean here? | A kind of window | A film about the sea | To look through glasses | *An opinion, or what you think
exercise: In maths, what is a plan view of a 3-D shape? | Its weight | Its colour | *How it looks from above | How it looks from the side
test: «She views it as a challenge.» What does views mean here? | To sell something cheaply | To look for a lost pet | To dance slowly | *To think about something in a certain way
test: «Move, you're blocking my view!» What does view mean here? | To watch a film with friends | An opinion about a book | A short walk to the shops | *The ability to see something from where you are
exam: Which sentence uses view as a verb? | Move, you're blocking my view! | The view from the hill was stunning | In my view, we should go home | *She will view the photos tonight
